<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Apple Privacy Manifest for the app target. Capacitor and Cordova ship their own for their
  frameworks (both declare nothing); this one covers the app's own bundle, and is where the
  declarations for any Capacitor plugin added later belong.

  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes is empty because nothing in the build uses a required-reason API.
  Checked on 2026-10-30 by scanning the Debug Simulator build's App, App.debug.dylib,
  Capacitor and Cordova binaries for the symbols and keys of the five categories (file
  timestamps, system boot time, disk space, active keyboard, UserDefaults): no references.
  There are no plugins today. Re-run that scan when one is added; each API it brings needs
  a declaration here with an approved reason code, and App Store Connect rejects an upload
  with an undeclared one (an automated email, after the build is processed).

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty on purpose. Companion Planning is a client for a
  server the person runs; what they enter is sent only to that server, which Lifescope has
  no access to, so under Apple's access-based definition the developer collects nothing.
  The App Store Connect "App Privacy" label is a separate artifact and the owner's to
  answer; keep the two in step. A demo server run by Lifescope for App Review would change
  this: data sent to it is developer-accessible and must then be declared here and on the
  label. The bundle makes no third-party request: Manrope ships inside it
  (client/src/fonts), so no font host is contacted.

  Tracking: none. No ads, no analytics SDK, no cross-app identifiers. The client reports
  errors only if VITE_SENTRY_DSN was baked in at build time, and the mobile build sets none.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
